Falsifies `system_tests::user::running_space_tests::a_builder_that_gave_its_scratch_up_faults_writing_to_a_childs_page`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect: the loader stops giving a scratch page up once the page is in the child, which is
what it did before milestone 95 (an unmap primitive) had a running space to unmap from. The
builder keeps a read/write window onto every page it built, exactly as the progenitor kept one
onto every boot server.

Expected to fail: in the run with its own space, the assertion that no second report arrives,
because the write landed and the witness said so.

diff --git a/crates/process_builder/src/lib.rs b/crates/process_builder/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/process_builder/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/process_builder/src/lib.rs
@@ -487,7 +487,7 @@
     // The page is written and in the child (or the build failed): either way this builder is done
     // with its own window onto it. Given up here, one page at a time, rather than after the child
     // is built, so the window is never wider than the page being filled.
-    give_up_own_page(scratch);
+    let _ = scratch;
     if mapped { Ok(()) } else { Err(()) }
 }
 
